WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.160
The Saw timeline is really well thought out.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:06.200
Despite the fact that there are constant flashbacks,
retcons and events being told out of order,

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.790
you can still piece together everything in
a way that makes sense.

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:11.469
Except for the history of this guy, Logan
Nelson.

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:15.549
If you want to see how Nelson breaks the timeline,
and my idea of how it can be fixed, then stick

00:00:15.549 --> 00:00:17.260
around to the end of this video.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:21.020
[INTRO]

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.210
Hello, and welcome to Horror History.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:27.439
My name The Professor -- not that Professor
-- Professor CZsWorld and in today’s lesson

00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:28.439
I’m talking Saw.

00:00:28.439 --> 00:00:32.580
More specifically, the most recent of Jigsaw’s
many disciples, Lieutenant Logan Nelson.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.000
Nelson made his debut in the eighth movie,
Jigsaw, and there are still unanswered questions

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.550
about his character that may be left open
for future installments, as hinted at by the

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:41.040
directors, The Spierig Brothers.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.290
I will talk about those possibilities, but
before we can get there, we’ve gotta take

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:47.040
it back to the debut of the first disciple.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:52.420
Logan Nelson was born on August 18th, 1973.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:57.640
He grew up to become a medic, and at 6”2’
195 lbs he was also a pretty big force to

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:58.640
be reckoned with.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:02.510
When Logan was 29, he was doing his residency
in Metropolitan City at The Angel of Mercy

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:06.690
Hospital, the same hospital that Dr. Lawrence
Gordon was treating a patient named John Kramer.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:11.000
One day in 2003 he was responsible for labeling
a couple of x-rays and accidentally switched

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.610
the labels, an event that prevented John’s
doctor from correctly diagnosing his brain

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:16.180
tumor in its early stages.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:19.610
That small mistake ended up being one of his
biggest mistakes, because it was this that

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:23.240
caused Kramer, who would one day become known
as “The Jigsaw Killer” to include Nelson

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.100
in his first ever game, a challenge that included
five contestants fighting for their lives

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.640
to prove that they cherish life.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:33.130
He is put into a room at a secluded barn with
four other wrongdoers, but the sedation used

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:36.760
on Logan doesn’t wear off at the same time
as the others, so by the time he wakes up,

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:39.730
he’s nearly already been pulled into a wall
of spinning saw blades.

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:43.479
He ends up getting cut by the blades, leaving
permanent scars on his back, but luckily,

00:01:43.479 --> 00:01:46.750
John realized that he didn’t have a fair
chance, and didn’t want him dying over an

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:50.360
honest mistake, so he ran out to save him
and give him a second chance.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:53.820
After stitching up his back, he made Nelson
his apprentice, teaching him Jigsaw’s moral

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.440
code and engineering techniques.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:59.070
Together, they built what would become known
as one of Jigsaw’s most iconic traps, the

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:01.380
reverse bear trap, and John would impress
the manta,

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.380
“we'll speak for the dead,”

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:04.770
which had a great impact on Nelson going forward.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:08.170
John’s partnership with Nelson would come
to an end however, later that year when Nelson

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:11.620
shipped out to serve in the military, where
he was a Lieutenant from May 2003 through

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:12.709
July of 2005.

00:02:12.709 --> 00:02:14.900
“Logan was our medic in Fallujah.”

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:19.110
Fallujah is short for Al-Fallujah, a city
in Iraq where two of the biggest battles of

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.900
America’s Iraq War took place.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:24.640
Keith Hunt also served in Fallujah, and mentions
that even as a medic, Nelson took out some

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.490
Taliban guys before being captured.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:30.300
He was tortured, possibly with hydrofluoric
acid, which he recognizes the effects of as

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.990
a medical examiner years later.

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:36.450
According to Nelson’s file, “he was imprisoned
Republican Guard loyalists for 5 months and

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.450
11 days.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:40.460
During his imprisonment, along with four other
members of his medical patrol, he was subjected

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:44.440
to an array for interrogation methods for
the purpose of discovering his unit’s plans

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:45.980
for the recapture of Fallujah.”

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:49.840
This is almost certainly where he developed
his stone cold demeanor, we see it later when

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.430
he’s being questioned by Keith Hunt and
of course at the end where he goes full punishment

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:54.430
mode.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:57.510
“Lieutenant Nelson was released in a prisoner
exchange brokered by army general Fitzpatrick

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:02.900
in May 2005 at which time he was transferred
to VISN5 (VA Capital Healthcare Network in

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:05.470
Maryland) where he received PTSD treatment
for 23 months.”

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:09.440
In other words, he was still jumping at shadows
after getting free, so they treated him in

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:12.630
a hospital for veterans from May 2005 until
April 2007.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.860
During that time,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:18.040
“Patient exhibited signs of extreme anxiety
and antisocial behavior for approximately

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.040
7 weeks,”

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.750
Much like me when I’m editing a video...

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:26.060
“during which Dr. Perry prescribed a regime
of Serotonin Reuptake Inhibitors (or SSRIs)

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:27.060
with limited success.”

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:31.010
We don’t know exactly when Logan met his
wife, but it seems like his daughter was conceived

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.819
in December of 2005 while he was still under
treatment.

00:03:33.819 --> 00:03:38.290
“Nelson was eventually released under his
own recognizance on August 9th 2006, but suffered

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:40.819
a severe relapse following the birth of his
daughter Melissa.

00:03:40.819 --> 00:03:44.230
Lieutenant Nelson lashed out at a neighbor
with a yard sign and was arrested following

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:47.720
an argument with his wife’s physician, in
which Logan repeatedly struck the doctor in

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:49.300
the head and was later sued for injuries.”

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.020
Man…

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:51.300
I wonder what the yard sign said.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.020
Go figure.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:55.709
Nelson considered himself a ‘broken man’
after the war.

00:03:55.709 --> 00:03:58.400
“Ten years ago I came out of the war a broken man.”

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.000
Yes.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:00.849
That’s what I just said.

00:04:00.849 --> 00:04:04.480
But Jigsaw helped him put the pieces of his
life back together again… like a Jigsaw

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:05.680
puzzle -- see what they did there?

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.239
Now this is where the timing of events gets
a little bit wonky, because I don’t really

00:04:09.239 --> 00:04:13.099
think Lieutenant Nelson linked up with Jigsaw
again after the war, long story short, because

00:04:13.099 --> 00:04:16.859
Jigsaw was pretty busy with some other stuff
at the time and he was dead by the time Nelson

00:04:16.859 --> 00:04:19.079
had his big relapse and yard sign incident.

00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:22.469
I think what Logan means with that line, is
that it was Jigsaw’s teachings that helped

00:04:22.469 --> 00:04:24.520
him eventually overcome the PTSD.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:27.409
There are some other possibilities, but I’ll
talk about those a little bit later.

00:04:27.409 --> 00:04:32.199
“He was readmitted to VISN5 on September
12, 2006 and improved steadily through the

00:04:32.199 --> 00:04:33.199
rest of the year.

00:04:33.199 --> 00:04:35.389
Nelson was re-released on December 12, 2006
and has since been considered medically clear,

00:04:35.389 --> 00:04:38.790
and has not been prescribed SSRIs since May
of 2007.”

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:43.539
He was released from the care of Dr. Angus
Perry on February 10th, 2007, and “his breakdown

00:04:43.539 --> 00:04:47.900
of the summer of 2006 is considered an aberration,
and Dr. Perry has signed off on his condition,

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:50.189
insisting that Nelson is not a threat to himself.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.680
He was awarded a purple heart on October 5th,
2007.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:57.880
So all of this, from 2003-2007, between being
in the war overseas and dealing with his own

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:02.139
mental illness battle back home, helps explain
why he, as one of Jigsaw’s disciples, wasn’t

00:05:02.139 --> 00:05:07.319
a factor during the seven Saw films, which
take place from 2004-2007, not including the

00:05:07.319 --> 00:05:08.319
flashbacks.

00:05:08.319 --> 00:05:11.020
To this point, an argument can be made for
the morality of Nelson’s character, but

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:15.099
what would happen after returning to the Metropolitan
area caused him to take an ever darker outlook

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:15.880
on life.

00:05:23.659 --> 00:05:27.130
Logan used his knowledge in the field of health
care to become a medical examiner not long

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:31.699
after the Jigsaw saga had concluded, but despite
Jigsaw leaving a lasting legacy on the city,

00:05:31.699 --> 00:05:35.940
criminals eventually started to run rampant
again and bodies continued to pile up.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:38.970
During his first year in county, the body
of an 8-year old girl showed up on Nelson’s

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:41.880
examination table, an event that he felt could
have been prevented.

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:45.139
It happened one day after Detective Halloran,
who I’m just now realizing I don’t know

00:05:45.139 --> 00:05:48.900
the first name of, captured a predator named
Alastor Shultz, and brought him in for questioning,

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:52.719
but during the interrogation got too rough,
resulting in Schultz getting off on a technicality

00:05:52.719 --> 00:05:55.240
where he quickly took his anger out on an
innocent young girl.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:58.649
Logan held this against Halloran for a long
time, which wasn’t helped by the fact that

00:05:58.649 --> 00:06:01.419
this was the first of many transgressions
on Halloran’s part.

00:06:01.419 --> 00:06:04.939
As innocent bodies continued to pile up on
Nelson’s table… well ok, they didn’t

00:06:04.939 --> 00:06:08.699
literally pile up, he looked at them one at
a time probably… but as the body count continued

00:06:08.699 --> 00:06:11.949
to grow, so did Nelson’s disgust for Detective
Halloran and his methods.

00:06:11.949 --> 00:06:15.509
He also called Halloran an impulsive ***hole
a couple times in the media, which created

00:06:15.509 --> 00:06:17.719
a tension between the two that everyone knew
about.

00:06:17.719 --> 00:06:21.020
It wasn’t just Halloran’s excessive use
of force that bothered Nelson though, he also

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:23.250
had a penchant for letting criminals off the
hook.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:27.129
The most notable example was Edgar Munsen,
a meth addict, thief and assaulter who wiggled

00:06:27.129 --> 00:06:29.619
out of two arrests because he was Halloran’s
informant.

00:06:29.619 --> 00:06:33.319
I’d cite the lack of discipline as a major
reason that Munsen never cleaned up his act

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:37.880
and ended up committing the most heinous crime
of all: putting ketchup on a hot dog.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:40.380
"The game's just getting started."

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:43.159
Nah, I’m just kidding, he ****ing murdered
Nelson’s wife.

00:06:43.159 --> 00:06:46.849
I think it was at this point that Nelson probably
started plotting his revenge.

00:06:46.849 --> 00:06:50.249
With Jigsaw’s words, “we speak for the
dead”, still echoing in his head, with his

00:06:50.249 --> 00:06:55.139
unique position as the county medical examiner
and with his close proximity to Halloran and

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:58.099
his department, Nelson began paying close
attention to the criminals that Halloran let

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.129
off of the hook.

00:06:59.129 --> 00:07:02.759
His aim was to recreate the game that Jigsaw
had placed him in all those years ago using

00:07:02.759 --> 00:07:06.309
criminals from Halloran’s botched cases
along with Halloran and himself.

00:07:06.309 --> 00:07:08.310
Nelson discovered his first candidate in 2011.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:12.099
A degenerate gambler named Malcolm Neale was
partially responsible for the death of his

00:07:12.099 --> 00:07:15.909
wife when the people he owed money to broke
into his home and slit Mrs. Neale’s throat.

00:07:15.909 --> 00:07:19.759
Halloran never managed to put him away for
the illegal gambling charges and Neale fit

00:07:19.759 --> 00:07:23.479
the profile of one of the guys from Jigsaw’s
original game at the barn, so Nelson took

00:07:23.479 --> 00:07:25.389
things into his own hands to punish him.

00:07:25.389 --> 00:07:28.719
Over the next five years, he kept his eyes
open and found two other criminals that he

00:07:28.719 --> 00:07:32.080
deemed similar to the other two contestants
of John’s game at the barn.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:35.270
In 2016 he abducted them and put them through
their own game.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:38.370
As expected, they made the same mistakes as
their predecessors did -- though it’s not

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:42.119
really clear if Nelson made the games winnable
like Jigsaw did, or if he was just torturing

00:07:42.119 --> 00:07:43.300
them to avenge the dead.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:47.580
The game began when Nelson abducted his wife’s
killer, Edgar Munsen and left him in an abandoned

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:51.991
warehouse with an audio tape created by splicing
together old archival audio of John Kramer

00:07:51.991 --> 00:07:55.550
to make it look like Jigsaw was back from
the dead and conducting a new game.

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:58.700
Surprisingly, it didn’t end up sounding
like a bad soundboard prank call.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:00.040
*dial tone*

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.300
"Thank you for calling the front desk, this is Jake, how can I help you?"

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:04.240
"Hello. Greetings."

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:06.280
"Oh **** wait,  you're the Saw dude!"

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:08.400
"There's a man in the room with you."

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:10.340
"Who's watching Saw? WTF?"

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.000
"Welcome to your rebirth."

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:15.200
"You think it's over just because I'm dead?"

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:18.809
The tape told Munsen he had to get to a certain
rooftop with a trigger that would start the

00:08:18.809 --> 00:08:19.809
next game.

00:08:19.809 --> 00:08:23.479
He arrived there, chased by police, and each
of them aimed to destroy the trigger not knowing

00:08:23.479 --> 00:08:27.710
that Nelson was watching from another rooftop
with a sniper, which he used to shoot Munsen

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:28.770
simultaneously.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:32.450
After using his inside access to obtain a
capsule of John Kramer’s blood and, he injects

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:36.099
it into Malcolm Neale’s fingernails before
putting the body on display in public for

00:08:36.099 --> 00:08:40.320
police to find, and ultimately bring back
to him to examine with his very lovely assistant,

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:41.390
Eleanor Bonneville.

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:44.910
In fact, he wisely allows her to be the one
to notice the Jigsaw piece he had cut out

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:46.000
of the victim’s head.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.190
She doesn’t notice the flash drive lodged
in his face, so Nelson makes sure the police

00:08:49.190 --> 00:08:51.120
know about it by bringing it to light himself.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:54.020
On the outside of it, the text reads: and
then there were four.

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:57.270
The drive contains an audio file, so why don’t
we roll it?

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:01.140
“The games have begun again.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:07.560
And they will not stop until the sins against
the innocent are atoned for.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:10.120
I will take care of the next four.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:12.490
You take care of the rest.”

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:16.130
Just as Jigsaw and his other apprentices did
during the Saw saga, Logan is leaving this

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:18.690
as a message directly for Detective Halloran.

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:22.470
That evening, Nelson would deposit the next
body from his recreated game at the Pig Farm.

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:25.490
This one was supposed to resemble a woman
named Carly from the original game.

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:28.950
He tosses her body from the rooftop of St.
Peter’s hospital, the same hospital where

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:31.440
Edgar Munsen is being treated for his gunshot
wound.

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:34.560
This time the body has a sign that says, “and
then there were three.”

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:37.990
The purpose of counting down like this is
to crank up the pressure on Detective Halloran

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:41.470
and force him to solve the mystery; to find
and put a stop to the game while there are

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:43.300
still living contestants to rescue.

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:46.500
However, it’s all a facade, because the
only two living contestants at this point

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:49.280
are Nelson himself
and Detective Halloran who is being lured

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:51.690
to the game’s location by this lie.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:55.310
Once again, Nelson is called in to examine
a corpse that he created, this time dropping

00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:59.360
more hints by pointing out the victim was
killed by hydrofluoric acid, not a rooftop

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:04.000
fall -- a nice little homage to one of Jigsaw’s
traps in Saw 6 where the same acid is used

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.050
in the game where William Easton is executed.

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:10.150
It’s also probably a satisfying act for
Nelson, who was also tortured with HF acid

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:12.410
during his time being imprisoned in the war.

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:15.890
Before the last member of the game is revealed,
something strange comes up with Nelson’s

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:19.000
assistant, Eleanor that completely changes
Logan’s plan.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:29.860
That night, Logan has to stay late at work,
and video chats his daughter and the babysitter

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:33.630
to say goodnight, highlighting what I think
is a possible weakness for him going forward.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.180
He clearly cares a lot about his daughter.

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:37.130
There’s only one Jigsaw apprentice of the
past who has a kid.

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:40.510
I’ll give you a clue, they used to work
at the same hospital together.

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:44.440
Lawrence Gordon found out how hard it is to
have your child taken hostage as part of Jigsaw’s

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:48.210
game way back in the first movie, but we’ve
also seen similar tactics used to manipulate

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:50.810
characters like Eric Matthews and Jeff Denlon.

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:54.270
After getting off the call, Detectives Halloran
and Hunt confront Nelson and explain that

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:55.270
his hot assistant…

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:59.200
I mean... his assistant... has been sending
a lot of web traffic to a website called Jigsaw

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:00.200
Rules.

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:03.410
And no, I’m not sure if it’s called that
because they’re fans of Jigsaw, you know,

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:06.490
like, “Ah yeah bruh, Jigsaw Rules, he’s
the best,” or if it’s more of a reference

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:09.960
to the fact that Jigsaw holds these games
where the rules have to be followed.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:11.780
"Why do you need Amanda in the game?"

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:13.740
“To ensure that the rules
are followed.”

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:17.530
It’s also unclear if all of that traffic
was coming from Eleanor, or if Logan was also

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:18.920
responsible for some of it.

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:23.310
Eleanor obviously used it for her weird hobby
of recreating Saw traps, but Logan could have

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:26.010
used it at some point as a resource for his
version of the barn game.

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:30.100
This is Logan’s intellect comes into play,
what makes him more dangerous than some of

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:31.100
Jigsaw’s former disciples.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:35.240
He’s able to turn this dangerous situation
into his advantage, and here’s how he does

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:36.240
it.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:40.080
First, he defends Eleanor, even though making
her a suspect could be advantageous for him.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:42.130
Instead, he uses reverse-psychology.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:45.600
By protecting Eleanor instead of himself,
he causes the detectives to actually become

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:46.870
more suspicious of her.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:51.000
It’s not 100% clear if he knew he was being
followed that night as he found Eleanor at

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:54.530
Brewer’s Moon and got her to take him to
her studio, a warehouse filled with her own

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:58.930
recreations of Jigsaw’s now famous traps,
but upon seeing this collection, Nelson realizes

00:11:58.930 --> 00:12:03.670
how he can further confuse Hunt, who is tailing
them, by muddying the clarity of the situation.

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:07.361
Eleanor shows him the human blender, which
he recognizes from Kramer’s barn game, but

00:12:07.361 --> 00:12:10.470
he plays dumb, telling her that no victims
died in anything like that.

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:13.380
It’s amazing that he was able to keep a
straight face through all of this, perhaps

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:17.570
highlighting his sociopathic tendencies, because
Logan already knew full well that the next

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:21.360
victim of his version of the barn game was
killed in a blender just like this one, so

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:24.180
he plotted to plant the next body in Eleanor’s
studio.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:25.970
He was especially busy that night though.

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:29.750
He also had time to kidnap Edgar Munsen from
the hospital under the nose of the sleeping

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:34.530
guard, and relocate his body into the tomb
of John Kramer, who was set to be dug up in

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:36.920
order to prove to the public that he was still
dead.

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:40.550
This of course, sent people into a frenzy,
lending more credence to the idea that the

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:43.240
original Jigsaw had returned from beyond the
grave.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:47.410
Logan never planned on Eleanor being a Jigsaw
fan-girl or Kramer’s body being dug up,

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:51.390
but he was able to stay calm and turn both
of these potential subversions into advantages.

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:54.780
And that’s what makes him such a scary carrier
of the Jigsaw legacy.

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:58.750
He’s able to suppress the rage that used
to get him in trouble after the war, and become

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:02.330
a collected, calculating psychopath, which
is my favorite kind of villain.

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:05.640
The next steps after that were pretty easy,
but would not be without a couple of challenges.

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:09.280
The most obvious was to plant the cut out
jigsaw pieces in Halloran’s freezer.

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:12.860
Remember, the goal isn’t to pin the crime
on Eleanor, she’s just a distraction for

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:13.860
the cops right now.

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:15.870
The real one to take the fall has to be Halloran.

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:19.600
Then, Keith Hunt shows up to arrest Nelson,
thinking he and Bonneville are in cahoots

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:21.190
together and killing the new victims.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:25.010
Again, he’s able to turn the situation on
it’s head by offering all he knows and essentially

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:27.730
making it look like Halloran is the one trying
to frame him.

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:31.730
He cites the evidence that lines up perfectly
with Halloran being guilty, because he set

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:35.380
everything up that way -- all of the victims
are Halloran’s old cases, and he gave the

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:39.440
order to shoot the remote that Munson was
holding way back… you know, when that happened.

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:42.260
Logan was the one who fired it, but nobody
knew he was even there.

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:46.800
In order to fully clear his name, Nelson suggests
they go back to the medical table and examine

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:47.800
Munson.

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:50.610
When Hunt isn’t looking, he switches the
bullet with one from Halloran’s gun.

00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:52.690
This is honestly kind of like the flimsiest
thing in the movie.

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:55.740
I mean the body has already been moved by
the killer this point, so I don’t see why

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:57.920
said killer couldn’t just switch the bullet
out.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:00.760
I guess Hunt didn’t think about that though,
cause it works.

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:05.420
Hunt takes Nelson home and starts to investigate
Halloran, giving our boy Nelson time to find

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:08.940
Eleanor… well, she finds him, with the news
that she’s discovered the location of the

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:09.940
game.

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:10.940
This is perfect for Logan.

00:14:10.940 --> 00:14:14.540
I think at this point he realizes that Halloran
is following him, all he has to do is let

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:18.680
Eleanor lead them to the barn, exactly where
he wants Halloran to be for the final round

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:19.680
of the game.

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:23.200
The one wild card here is Ms. Bonneville,
so he’s gotta find a way to get rid of her

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:25.940
for a little while to give him time to deal
with Halloran.

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:29.350
Once again, Nelson finds a way to turn this
problem into a positive by convincing her

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:31.910
that Halloran is the killer and engaging in
a fight with him.

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:35.930
He tells Eleanor to run, before drugging Halloran
and taking him to the slaughter room.

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:39.980
Now he has one more person believing what
he wants them to believe, someone he probably

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:41.779
wasn’t even counting on being involved.

00:14:41.779 --> 00:14:46.250
The final round of the game is no game at
all, it’s a trap, but unlike John Kramer’s

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:47.680
traps, this one is inescapable.

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:50.840
He poses himself inside the room opposite
the detective.

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:54.510
Fabricated audio of John Kramer’s voice
tells them that they can escape death if they

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:56.690
admit the reason they deserve to die.

00:14:56.690 --> 00:15:00.210
The whole thing is a setup to get Halloran
to admit to being a dirty cop.

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:01.850
All Nelson has to do is sell it.

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:05.120
So he gives Halloran the chance to choose
who makes their confession first.

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:08.850
Letting him choose is secretly the ultimate
power move, because if he chooses himself,

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:12.480
he’ll probably confess, but if he presses
Logan’s button, he can sell the scenario

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:16.060
even further, because his collar is equipped
with fake lasers and fake blood.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:19.840
So that’s exactly what he does, he fakes
his death in order to scare Halloran into

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:21.162
making his confession, a confession that Nelson
has a recording of.

00:15:21.162 --> 00:15:25.321
A confession of tampering with evidence, taking
bribes, putting away innocent people, letting

00:15:25.321 --> 00:15:29.180
the worst criminals walk free and letting
innocent people die.

00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:33.710
More than enough to convince most people that
Halloran is the one behind the 2016 killings.

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:37.870
With that evidence, Logan no longer needs
his rival, and after explaining his plan like

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:41.980
a typical villain, he activates the real laser
cutters and executes Detective Halloran.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:45.300
If anyone knows where I can get one of those
things, I would love to have it to cut my

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:46.300
grapefruit.

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:48.520
So remember how I said there was an issue
with Nelson’s timeline?

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:49.520
Yeah.

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:50.860
There’s an issue with Nelson’s timeline.

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:52.800
Let’s see if we can make some sense of it.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:03.860
Throughout Jigsaw, characters are constantly
going around saying that Jigsaw can’t be

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:06.390
back, he’s been dead for 10 years.

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:07.480
"Kramer's been dead for 10 years."

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:09.720
"John Kramer's dead, and has been for 10 years."

00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:10.810
See.

00:16:10.810 --> 00:16:11.810
I told you.

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:16.050
That’s why I’ve been saying that Nelson’s
game takes place in 2016, 10 years after Jigsaw’s

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:17.050
death in 2006.

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:20.710
But at the end of the movie, when Logan does
his evil villain speech, he says that John’s

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:26.480
original game, which he did as a secret test
before all the other games, was 10 years ago.

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:28.740
"Ten years ago in this very barn...

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.520
...a game was played."

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:38.880
Well the first game was in 2004, so it can’t
be 10 years since 2004 *and* 10 years since

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:40.710
2006 simultaneously.

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:42.470
Not if both games are on Earth anyway.

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:45.529
The other confusing thing is that Nelson says
Jigsaw helped put him back together his life

00:16:45.529 --> 00:16:46.529
after the war.

00:16:46.529 --> 00:16:50.510
You may remember he didn’t start to recover
until September 2006, which is actually after

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:51.510
Jigsaw died.

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:54.880
So all of this doesn’t quite add up as neatly
as the seven Saw films.

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:56.630
But there may be a simple explanation.

00:16:56.630 --> 00:17:00.610
Well, the simplest explanation is that they
****ed up, but there may be a canon explanation

00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:01.610
as well.

00:17:01.610 --> 00:17:02.630
There are two options really.

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:05.839
The first is that the game at the barn didn’t
really take place before the bathroom game

00:17:05.839 --> 00:17:07.309
in October 2004.

00:17:07.309 --> 00:17:10.929
It is stated that Jigsaw’s barn game took
place before all the other games, but what

00:17:10.929 --> 00:17:15.009
if it only took place before all the other
games that the public actually knows about?

00:17:15.009 --> 00:17:18.890
The earliest known game would be The Nerve
Gas house in Saw II, which happens in October

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:20.039
2005.

00:17:20.039 --> 00:17:24.110
That gets us pretty close to 10 years, it
would actually be 11 years in 2016, but it’s

00:17:24.110 --> 00:17:27.709
easier to clump the game and the rest of John’s
life together as one event if you do it like

00:17:27.709 --> 00:17:28.709
that.

00:17:28.709 --> 00:17:31.999
But there is one snag in that theory, which
is that Eleanor’s studio has a replica of

00:17:31.999 --> 00:17:33.140
the hacksaw from the bathroom.

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:35.390
You know, the one Gordon used to escape.

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:38.880
Which means the public did find out about
the bathroom at some point.

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:41.789
So the barn game probably took place before
the bathroom game.

00:17:41.789 --> 00:17:45.320
There’s also the fact that we see Logan
and John building the reverse bear trap together,

00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:48.769
and the reverse bear trap is invented even
earlier than that bathroom game.

00:17:48.769 --> 00:17:51.110
We see Amanda tested by it in May of 2004.

00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:55.179
That’s why I made this video under the idea
that Jigsaw’s barn game took place shortly

00:17:55.179 --> 00:17:59.590
after Logan Nelson switched John’s x-rays
in 2003, and Logan Nelson’s barn game took

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:02.720
place 10 years after Jigsaw’s death in 2006.

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:06.710
This makes the information on Nelson’s file
fit nicely into the series, because it perfectly

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:11.899
explains why Nelson never helped John during
Saw 1-7: he was at war for part of it, and

00:18:11.899 --> 00:18:14.179
busy being treated for PTSD for the other
part.

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:15.180
As for Nelson’s line,

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:18.480
"Ten years ago in this very barn... a game was played."

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:20.860
I think it’s possible that he was just generalizing.

00:18:20.860 --> 00:18:23.389
He was essentially saying, “this was all
about a decade ago.”

00:18:23.389 --> 00:18:26.340
It’s not like he’s been counting year
by year, but he knows it’s been at least

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:29.759
10 years since John Kramer's barn game and
about 10 years since his death.

00:18:29.759 --> 00:18:33.409
The last retort that Halloran tries is when
he points out the fact that John Kramer gave

00:18:33.409 --> 00:18:35.330
victims a choice to try to win the game.

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:37.331
And Nelson’s response to that is just savage.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:38.331
Roll that ****.

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:42.399
“You have a choice.

00:18:42.399 --> 00:18:44.499
Scream or don’t.”

00:18:44.499 --> 00:18:48.620
So Nelson actually ends up committing the
murder himself, unlike Jigsaw, but a lot like

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:51.730
some of the other failed disciples like Amanda
and Hoffman.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:54.240
Logan Nelson is both a warrior and a tactician.

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:58.549
Once groomed to be the next successor to Jigsaw,
things went horribly wrong when his rehabilitation

00:18:58.549 --> 00:19:00.669
was interrupted by service in the military.

00:19:00.669 --> 00:19:04.340
The post-traumatic stress that is often a
symptom of mental illness in army veterans

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:08.669
ended up warping and distorting his still
rehabilitating mind into a sociopath and psychopath

00:19:08.669 --> 00:19:11.139
-- the likes of which we’ve seen before.

00:19:11.139 --> 00:19:15.039
Combine that with his scary physicality and
extremely sharp and fast acting intelligence,

00:19:15.039 --> 00:19:18.740
and we could have one of the scariest villains
in the Saw franchise going forward.

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:23.090
At the end of Jigsaw, the only confirmed survivors
among Jigsaw’s successors are Logan Nelson,

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:26.570
who has strayed from the path of John’s
teaching, and Lawrence Gordon, who has protected

00:19:26.570 --> 00:19:28.760
his legacy for the last 12 years.

00:19:28.760 --> 00:19:32.500
Both are medical masterminds who have also
taken on the arts of mechanical engineering

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:34.119
and deductive reasoning.

00:19:34.119 --> 00:19:38.269
One has the advantage of brute force and military
background, and the other has 10 times the

00:19:38.269 --> 00:19:42.190
experience being Jigsaw and two unknown apprentices
helping him out.

00:19:42.190 --> 00:19:46.409
Hopefully we get to see these two masterminds
battle it out, Jigsaw vs. Jigsaw in a future

00:19:46.409 --> 00:19:47.409
movie.

00:19:47.409 --> 00:19:50.600
It would be an epic battle that forever changes
the franchise going forward.

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:53.289
So that’s it SO FAR for the history of Logan
Nelson.

00:19:53.289 --> 00:19:57.100
